From f714b00ad19bbce5b662ade07ff23db243e0d602 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marivi Fernandez-Serra <Marivi.Fernandez-Serra@stonybrook.edu>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 16:33:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] XClib: machine-learned LDA/GGA/meta-GGA functionals through
 libnxc (input_dft='NXC')

- xc_nxc.f90: calls libnxc's Fortran module (nxc) for the whole functional; model
  directory from $NXC_MODEL, family (LDA_/GGA_/MGGA_) from its name.  Conventions of
  the XClib wrappers (Hartree; LDA energy per particle, GGA/MGGA energy per volume,
  v2 = 2 dE/dsigma_ss, v2c_ud / meta v2c cross terms, tau in Libxc units); LSDA
  (rho, m) converted as in QE's LSDA drivers.
- intercepts in xc (LDA family), xc_gcx (GGA family) and xc_metagcx (meta-GGA);
  PBE/TPSS indices are set only as placeholders so that PW computes gradients/tau;
  dmxc/dgcxc (DFPT) stop with an error for NXC.
- CMake: -DQE_ENABLE_NXC=ON -DNXC_ROOT=<libnxc build/install>.

Validated with analytic twins through libnxc (Slater, QE's PBE, Libxc PKZB and LTA
meta-GGA exchange) against QE-native / QE+Libxc runs: Si, BN, Mo, ferromagnetic
Fe and an N atom; energies, forces and stresses agree (to 1e-8 Ry where QE's own
thresholds do not differ).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
